<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span><span id="A6.T7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training-step efficiency on OWT</span> (<math id="A6.T7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1024,V=65{,}536" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65,536</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1024,V=65{,}536</annotation></semantics></math>).
The dense <math id="A6.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BTV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BTV</annotation></semantics></math> logit tensor pushes the token baseline close to the single-GPU memory limit by batch size 64, whereas the bitstream model remains substantially lighter and faster.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>End-to-end generation sweeps</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A6.T8" title="In F.3 End-to-end generation sweeps ‣ Appendix F Computational and Memory Efficiency ‣ Towards Closing the Autoregressive Gap in Language Modeling via Entropy-Gated Continuous Bitstream Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tables</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and <a href="#A6.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ F.3 End-to-end generation sweeps ‣ Appendix F Computational and Memory Efficiency ‣ Towards Closing the Autoregressive Gap in Language Modeling via Entropy-Gated Continuous Bitstream Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> show generation-time scaling at 128 NFEs for batches <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\geq 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\geq 16</annotation></semantics></math>.
Throughput is measured in completed generated semantic tokens per second and includes the full denoising trajectory.
The bitstream advantage grows with batch size because the token-space model repeatedly materializes <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\times T\times V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\times T\times V</annotation></semantics></math> logits at every denoising evaluation, whereas Bitstream Diffusion materializes only <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\times T\times\lceil\log_{2}V\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\times T\times\lceil\log_{2}V\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> bit logits.
The effect is especially pronounced on OWT, where <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1024</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=65{,}536" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65,536</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=65{,}536</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
